# Line endings: LF in the index, Windows CRLF in the working copy, for every text file.
#
# The author works on Windows and wants every file on disk in Windows format. An explicit eol
# attribute wins over each machine's core.autocrlf, so the repo says so itself and Git does not
# show a working copy of CRLF files as modified. The index stays LF (it always has been), so
# this changes checkout only: no history rewrite and no line-ending churn in diffs.
# .editorconfig says end_of_line = crlf to match, so editors save the same way.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Real binary assets: never line-ending converted, never diffed as text.
# Of these, only .png is tracked today (265 sprite sheets); the rest guard assets
# that are expected to land here (fonts, audio, built .xnb) and any local-only ROM dump.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.xnb binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
ref/rom/robotron64k.bin binary
